+
+### Effective model facts versus safety defaults
+
+The global `modelMatch: ".*"` rule exists to complete the current runtime contract, but its
+200K context, 32K output, tool support and enabled/disabled effort choices are not provider
+metadata. Keep that runtime fallback until the transport contract can represent unknowns. Add a
+read-only sparse evidence projection from the existing ordered model-rule owner: exact provider
+observations, explicit personal corrections and model-specific built-in recommendations count;
+unqualified wildcard rules do not. Settings must show a value only when that field has evidence,
+and mark built-in recommendations separately from provider-reported data. Unknown remains unknown
+in the model row/editor and must not be advertised as an actual context capacity. The runtime
+fallback remains traceable and is never written into personal corrections by viewing/editing a
+model. No new model store, inferred entitlement or paid test is introduced.
